{# "Patrols — the whole column": the module's ENTIRE overview section as one
   widget, its heading and its cards, stacked. The "Module columns" direction is
   a page made of these, one per installed module.

   IT INCLUDES THE MODULE'S OWN PARTIALS AND RESTATES NOTHING. That is the rule
   the host's contributor interface leaves to the module to keep — "a column may
   only include widgets the module already contributes on their own, so a card
   can never read differently in the two" — and including is the only way to keep
   it. There is one _w_pl_now in this bundle, and whether it is drawn on its own
   or inside this column, it is that one.

   The includes carry `_context` with `with_context: false`, so each card reads
   exactly the map the host handed this one — the same `by.patrols` reading, not
   a second measurement.

   `.ao-col` and `.ao-colstack` are the HOST's column vocabulary; this module
   only colours its own dot. #}
{% set pl = by.patrols %}
<div data-w="pl_column">
    <div class="ao-col">
        <i class="patrols"></i>
        <b>Patrols</b>
        <span class="n">{{ pl.out|length }} out · {{ pl.today.closed }} closed today</span>
        <a href="{{ pl.dashboardUrl }}">Open the module →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="ao-colstack">
        {{ include('@UhifadhiLabsPatrol/overview/_w_pl_now.html.twig', _context, with_context = false) }}
        {{ include('@UhifadhiLabsPatrol/overview/_w_pl_today.html.twig', _context, with_context = false) }}
        {{ include('@UhifadhiLabsPatrol/overview/_w_pl_gaps.html.twig', _context, with_context = false) }}
    </div>
</div>
